  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 221 AM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nBy Saturday, an upper level low tracks across southern New Mexico, \nwith zonal flow in the northern stream across North Dakota. Subtle \nupper level ridging is expected to develop across the northern jet \nstream through the weekend. With the upper level ridging, warmer \ntemperatures aloft track across the region, bringing warmer \nconditions at the surface. Highs this weekend are expected to push \ninto the mid 60s, though there still is potential for a few \nlocations to reach the upper 60s. This would be around 10 degrees \nwarmer than usual, as typical highs for this time of year are the \nmid 50s. Lows this weekend drop into the mid to upper 30s, which \nremains warmer than usual, as typical lows are in the mid 20s. \n\nBy Monday, a shortwave tracks across the northern Plains, but should \nstill have limited impacts on temperatures. Highs are still expected \nto push into the mid 60s on Monday. By Tuesday, however, slightly \ncooler air aloft (around 11 degC) tracks into the region following \nthe shortwave, which may bring a slight cool off, with highs in the \nlower 60s and possibly upper 50s in locations. The northern jet \nstream remains north of the region, as upper level ridging begins to \ndevelop again with warmer temperatures aloft returning (around 14 \ndegC). This should bring a return of similar conditions to this \nweekend, with highs returning to the mid 60s. With upper level \nridging expected throughout most of the period, this should limit \nany precipitation chances from this weekend into the middle of next \nweek.",
